What does this Vitest code do?

```ts
it.each([
  [1, 1, 2],
  [2, 3, 5],
])('add(%i, %i) = %i', (a, b, sum) => {
  expect(add(a, b)).toBe(sum)
})
```

How many tests does pytest report for this?

```python
@pytest.mark.parametrize("a, b, total", [
    (1, 1, 2),
    (2, 3, 5),
    (0, 0, 0),
])
def test_add(a, b, total):
    assert add(a, b) == total
```
